    <string name="onboarding_page">Page %1$d of %2$d</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_title">Ethernet tethering, your way</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_text">EtherTether starts Android\'s own Ethernet tethering for a USB or USB-C Ethernet adapter: with a fixed address you choose, for devices such as diagnostic interfaces or lab equipment, or with normal sharing. Stop puts everything back to normal.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_shizuku_title">Shizuku gives the access</string>
    <string name="onboarding_shizuku_text">Android lets only the system and the debugging shell start tethering with a fixed address. Shizuku, a free separate app, runs with the shell\'s rights after you start it with wireless debugging, on the phone alone, no computer needed.</string>
